# Resolution Log: Voice Integration & Scoping
Task IDs: lgcc-agent-integration, voice-assistant-dispatch
Date: 2026-10-15
Author: Yassine

## Resolution Details
1. lgcc-agent-integration:
   - Voice transcription is implemented cleanly via `:Listen` (using faster-whisper from ~/myenv).
   - `:Lgcc` is implemented as an asynchronous Neovim command with live ticker and Quickfix on demand.
   - Voice readback of lgcc results is supported via `:Lgcc -s` using piper TTS.
   - Verified that :v was scrapped due to conflict with Vim visual mode / :vglobal commands.

2. voice-assistant-dispatch:
   - Formally retired / scrapped: user decision confirmed that speech-to-speech assistant mode is discarded.
   - `:Listen` is strictly reserved for continuous and push-to-talk voice transcription directly into the active buffer at cursor.
   - LLM logic checking remains strictly text/file-based via `:Lgcc`.
